Kebab keeps console output alive when the graphics console is paused.

printf goes through _cnputs, which returns early once initialize_screen() pauses
the graphics console. On this port the panel is the only console, so every
printf - including load_init_program's load attempts - was silently dropped
while kprintf kept working, which made real progress look like a hang.

--- a/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
+++ b/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
@@ -289,9 +289,15 @@
 {
 	extern int disableConsoleOutput;
 
+#if !defined(KEBAB)
+	/*
+	 * stock code drops console output while the graphics console is paused;
+	 * on this port the panel is the only console, so keep it always on.
+	 */
 	if (disableConsoleOutput) {
 		return;
 	}
+#endif
 
 	assert(c != NULL);
 
